PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L06U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":6,"cefr":"B1b","unit":4,"theme":"Mysteries","essential_question":"How do we find the truth when things are not what they seem?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1","title":"Someone Had Opened the Case: The Past Perfect","objectives":["Students will be able to form the past perfect with had + past participle.","Students will be able to use the past perfect to show which of two past actions happened first.","I can say \"When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.\"","I can ask \"Had anyone visited the library?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الماضي التام بـ had + التصريف الثالث.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الماضي التام لبيان أي حدثين ماضيين وقع أولًا.","أستطيع أن أقول When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.","أستطيع أن أسأل Had anyone visited the library?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mystery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɪstɚi/","definition":"something strange that nobody can explain","arabic":"لُغز / غموض","example":"The disappearance of the ship is still a mystery.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"clue","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klu/","definition":"a piece of information that helps you find an answer","arabic":"دليل / مفتاح للحل","example":"The detective found an important clue.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"detective","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈtɛktɪv/","definition":"a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries","arabic":"محقّق","example":"The detective asked everyone questions.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"suspect","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səˈspɛkt/","definition":"a person who might have done something wrong","arabic":"مشتبه به","example":"The police questioned three suspects.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use the past perfect for an action that happened before another action in the past. It's \"the past of the past\": When Noura arrived (2nd), someone had opened the case (1st).\nForm: had + past participle for all subjects: I/you/he/she/we/they had opened. Negative: hadn't + past participle. Question: Had + subject + past participle?\nCommon words: already, just, never, before, by the time: By the time the police came, the thief had already escaped. If the order is clear (with after or before), the past simple is also fine: After he ate / had eaten, he left.\nhad + past participle (all subjects)\npast perfect = the earlier action; past simple = the later action\nhadn't + past participle • Had + subject + past participle?\nby the time / already / just / never / before + past perfect","examples":["When I got home, my brother had eaten all the cake.","By the time the firefighters arrived, the fire had gone out.","She realized that she had left her phone on the bus.","I had never seen a falcon up close before that day.","The detective hadn't found any evidence.","Had the thief broken the lock?","We were tired because we had walked for hours.","After they had searched the house, they called the police."],"common_errors":["✗ When I arrived, the film already started. → ✓ When I arrived, the film had already started. (Earlier action → past perfect.)","✗ She had went home. → ✓ She had gone home. (had + past participle.)","✗ I didn't had eaten. → ✓ I hadn't eaten. (Negative: hadn't + past participle.)","✗ Did you had seen him before? → ✓ Had you seen him before? (Question: Had + subject + past participle.)"],"arabic":"الماضي التام had + التصريف الثالث لحدث وقع قبل حدث آخر في الماضي («ماضي الماضي»).\nWhen Noura arrived, someone had opened the case = عندما وصلت نورة، كان شخص ما قد فتح الخزانة.\nالنفي hadn't + التصريف الثالث، والسؤال Had + الفاعل + التصريف الثالث؟\nكلمات شائعة: already وjust وnever وby the time."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Someone Had Opened the Case: The Past Perfect”. Let’s learn the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U4-LS1 | Someone Had Opened the Case: The Past Perfect","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The Case of the Missing Manuscript”: When Noura arrived at the school library on Tuesday, she knew something was wrong. Someone had opened the glass case in the corner, and the old manuscript was gone! Look at the green words.","on_screen":"When Noura arrived at the school library on Tuesday, she knew something was wrong. Someone had opened the glass case in the corner, and the old manuscript was gone!","visual":"Image GV-L06-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use the past perfect for an action that happened before another action in the past. It's \"the past of the past\": When Noura arrived (2nd), someone had opened the case (1st). Form: had + past participle for all subjects: I/you/he/she/we/they had opened. Negative: hadn't + past participle. Question: Had + subject + past participle?","on_screen":"had + past participle (all subjects) • past perfect = the earlier action; past simple = the later action • hadn't + past participle • Had + subject + past participle?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. When I got home, my brother had eaten all the cake. By the time the firefighters arrived, the fire had gone out. She realized that she had left her phone on the bus.","on_screen":"When I got home, my brother had eaten all the cake. / By the time the firefighters arrived, the fire had gone out. / She realized that she had left her phone on the bus.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “When I arrived, the film already started.” That’s not right. We say: “When I arrived, the film had already started.” Earlier action → past perfect.","on_screen":"✗ When I arrived, the film already started.   ✓ When I arrived, the film had already started.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.\" What happened first? … Think! … Someone opened the case. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الماضي التام had + التصريف الثالث لحدث وقع قبل حدث آخر في الماضي («ماضي الماضي»).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: When I arrived, the film already started. — الصحيح: When I arrived, the film had already started.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Case of the Missing Manuscript","body":"When Noura arrived at the school library on Tuesday, she knew something was wrong. Someone had opened the glass case in the corner, and the old manuscript was gone!\nThe librarian, Ms. Huda, was sure that she had locked the case the evening before.\nNoura looked around carefully. Someone had left sandy footprints near the window. The window was open, but Ms. Huda said nobody had opened it all week because of the dust storms.\n\"Had anyone visited the library after school?\" Noura asked.\n\"Only Adam,\" Ms. Huda replied. \"He had forgotten his science book.\"\nAdam looked puzzled. \"I hadn't touched anything!\" he said. \"But I saw the cleaner's cat. It had climbed onto the case and was scratching the glass.\"\nThen Noura found the clue that solved the mystery: a note from the assistant librarian. The cat had knocked the case open, so he had moved the manuscript to a locked cupboard to keep it safe. The footprints were his – he had walked in from the sandy playground.\n\"Mystery solved!\" Noura said with a smile.","word_count":177,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"When we got to the station, the train ___.","options":["had already leave","already leaves","had already left","has already left"],"answer":"had already left","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"She was hungry because she ___ breakfast.","options":["didn't ate","hadn't eaten","hasn't eaten","hadn't eat"],"answer":"hadn't eaten","explanation":"hadn't + past participle.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"___ you ever ridden a camel before the trip?","options":["Were","Had","Did","Have"],"answer":"Had","explanation":"Had + subject + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"By the time the detective arrived, the suspect ___.","options":["had disappeared","has disappeared","had disappear","disappears"],"answer":"had disappeared","explanation":"by the time / already / never + past perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"I realized that I ___ my keys at school.","options":["had left","leave","have left","had leaved"],"answer":"had left","explanation":"had + past participle (gone, seen, left).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة."},{"q":"The house was dark because everyone ___ to bed.","options":["has gone","goes","had went","had gone"],"answer":"had gone","explanation":"had + past participle (gone, seen, left).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the past perfect. Word bank: had started, hadn't checked, had taken","items":[{"q":"When Omar opened the box, someone ______ (take) the money.","options":[],"answer":"had taken","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"We were late because we ______ (not / check) the time.","options":[],"answer":"hadn't checked","explanation":"hadn't + past participle.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"By the time I found my seat, the play ______ (start).","options":[],"answer":"had started","explanation":"by the time / already / never + past perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"When I arrived, my friends already ate dinner.","options":[],"answer":"When I arrived, my friends had already eaten dinner.","explanation":"already ate → had already eaten. Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: already ate → had already eaten. الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"She had wrote the answer before the bell rang.","options":[],"answer":"She had written the answer before the bell rang.","explanation":"had wrote → had written. had + past participle (gone, seen, left).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: had wrote → had written. الصيغة."},{"q":"Did you had heard the story before?","options":[],"answer":"Had you heard the story before?","explanation":"Did you had → Had you. Had + subject + past participle?","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Did you had → Had you. السؤال."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Finish the sentences with the past perfect.","items":[{"q":"When I got home yesterday, ___.","options":[],"answer":"When I got home yesterday, my mother had cooked my favorite dish.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I was tired because ___.","options":[],"answer":"I was tired because I had studied all night.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"By the time we reached the beach, ___.","options":[],"answer":"By the time we reached the beach, the sun had set.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I had never ___ before last year.","options":[],"answer":"I had never flown in a plane before last year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The teacher was angry because ___.","options":[],"answer":"The teacher was angry because we hadn't done our homework.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Detective's notebook.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 clues a detective found, using the past perfect.","options":[],"answer":"Someone had broken the window. The thief had worn gloves. He had left a red scarf behind.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 questions a detective asked, using Had…?","options":[],"answer":"Had you seen this man before? Had anyone opened the safe?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with by the time.","options":[],"answer":"By the time the police arrived, the thief had escaped.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions.","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"When I arrived, someone had…"},{"label":"By the time…, … had already…"},{"label":"I realized that I had…"},{"label":"She hadn't…"},{"label":"Had you…?"},{"label":"after he had…"},{"label":"It was raining when…"},{"label":"While we were…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"When I woke up, the snow ___.","options":["stops","had stop","had stopped","has stopped"],"answer":"had stopped","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"","options":["They haven't heard the news when I called.","They hadn't heard the news when I called.","They hadn't hear the news when I called.","They didn't had heard the news when I called."],"answer":"They hadn't heard the news when I called.","explanation":"hadn't + past participle.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"","options":["Did the thief had broken the window?","Had the thief broken the window?","Has the thief broken the window yesterday?","Had the thief broke the window?"],"answer":"Had the thief broken the window?","explanation":"Had + subject + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"By the time we arrived, the shop ___.","options":["had closed","had close","closes","has closed"],"answer":"had closed","explanation":"by the time / already / never + past perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"Lina ___ never seen snow before her trip to Turkey.","options":["has","did","was","had"],"answer":"had","explanation":"by the time / already / never + past perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"The witness said she ___ a man in a black jacket.","options":["sees","has seen","had saw","had seen"],"answer":"had seen","explanation":"had + past participle (gone, seen, left).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة."},{"q":"Which action happened first? \"When the guests arrived, Mom had cooked dinner.\"","options":["We don't know.","The guests arrived.","Mom cooked dinner.","Both at the same time."],"answer":"Mom cooked dinner.","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"I couldn't get into the house because I ___ my key.","options":["had lost","have lost","had lose","lose"],"answer":"had lost","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"","options":["After he had finished his homework, he plays football yesterday.","After he has finished his homework, he played football.","After he had finish his homework, he played football.","After he had finished his homework, he played football."],"answer":"After he had finished his homework, he played football.","explanation":"had + past participle (gone, seen, left).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة."},{"q":"The room was a mess. Someone ___ through all the drawers.","options":["searches","has searched","had searched","had search"],"answer":"had searched","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"The school library in the early morning: an empty glass case with its door open, sandy footprints near an open window, Noura with a notebook and a magnifying glass, Ms. Huda looking worried, and a ginger cat peeking from behind a shelf. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"The school library in the early morning: an empty glass case with its door open, sandy footprints near an open window, Noura with a notebook and a magnifying glass, Ms. Huda looking worried, and a ginger cat peeking from behind a shelf"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mystery (something strange that nobody can explain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mystery: something strange that nobody can explain"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows clue (a piece of information that helps you find an answer); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing clue: a piece of information that helps you find an answer"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows detective (a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing detective: a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows suspect (a person who might have done something wrong); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing suspect: a person who might have done something wrong"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W01","script":"mystery. mystery. The disappearance of the ship is still a mystery.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W02","script":"clue. clue. The detective found an important clue.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W03","script":"detective. detective. The detective asked everyone questions.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-W04","script":"suspect. suspect. The police questioned three suspects.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-T1","script":"When Noura arrived at the school library on Tuesday, she knew something was wrong. Someone had opened the glass case in the corner, and the old manuscript was gone! The librarian, Ms. Huda, was sure that she had locked the case the evening before. Noura looked around carefully. Someone had left sandy footprints near the window. The window was open, but Ms. Huda said nobody had opened it all week because of the dust storms. \"Had anyone visited the library after school?\" Noura asked. \"Only Adam,\" Ms. Huda replied. \"He had forgotten his science book.\" Adam looked puzzled. \"I hadn't touched anything!\" he said. \"But I saw the cleaner's cat. It had climbed onto the case and was scratching the glass.\" Then Noura found the clue that solved the mystery: a note from the assistant librarian. The cat had knocked the case open, so he had moved the manuscript to a locked cupboard to keep it safe. The footprints were his – he had walked in from the sandy playground. \"Mystery solved!\" Noura said with a smile.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Someone Had Opened the Case: The Past Perfect”. Let’s learn the past perfect (had + past participle) for an action that happened before another past action; already, just, never, by the time; negatives and questions together. Listen to the start of “The Case of the Missing Manuscript”: When Noura arrived at the school library on Tuesday, she knew something was wrong. Someone had opened the glass case in the corner, and the old manuscript was gone! Look at the green words. Use the past perfect for an action that happened before another action in the past. It's \"the past of the past\": When Noura arrived (2nd), someone had opened the case (1st). Form: had + past participle for all subjects: I/you/he/she/we/they had opened. Negative: hadn't + past participle. Question: Had + subject + past participle? Here are some examples. When I got home, my brother had eaten all the cake. By the time the firefighters arrived, the fire had gone out. She realized that she had left her phone on the bus. Be careful! Some learners say: “When I arrived, the film already started.” That’s not right. We say: “When I arrived, the film had already started.” Earlier action → past perfect. Quick check: \"When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.\" What happened first? … Think! … Someone opened the case. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"When Noura arrived, someone had opened the case.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2","title":"It Was Raining When… Narrative Tenses","objectives":["Students will be able to use the past simple, past continuous and past perfect together in a story.","Students will be able to choose when or while to connect background and main events.","I can say \"I was reading when the lights went out.\"","I can tell a story in the right order with three past tenses."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الماضي البسيط والماضي المستمر والماضي التام معًا في القصة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار when أو while لربط أحداث الخلفية بالأحداث الرئيسة.","أستطيع أن أقول I was reading when the lights went out.","أستطيع أن أروي قصة بالترتيب الصحيح بثلاثة أزمنة ماضية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"evidence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛvədəns/","definition":"facts or things that show something is true","arabic":"دليل / بيِّنة","example":"There wasn't enough evidence.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"witness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɪtnəs/","definition":"a person who saw something happen","arabic":"شاهد","example":"A witness saw a man running away.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"solve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɑlv/","definition":"to find the answer to a problem or mystery","arabic":"يحلّ","example":"Noura solved the mystery in one day.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"disappear","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌdɪsəˈpɪr/","definition":"to go away suddenly so you can't see it","arabic":"يختفي","example":"My pen disappeared from my desk.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Stories use three past tenses. The past simple tells the main events in order: The lights went out. Someone knocked on the door.\nThe past continuous (was/were + -ing) describes the background or an action in progress when something else happened: It was raining. I was reading when the lights went out. Use while + past continuous for a longer action: While we were walking home, we heard a noise.\nThe past perfect goes back in time to an earlier event: When I checked, someone had cut the wire. Use when + past simple for the short, interrupting action, and while + past continuous for the long, background action.\npast simple → main events in order\npast continuous → background / action in progress\npast perfect → earlier event (flashback)\nwhen + short action • while + long action","examples":["The wind was blowing, and the trees were shaking.","I was sleeping when I heard a strange sound.","While Saad was talking on the phone, someone took his bag.","When we opened the door, we saw that someone had moved the furniture.","She was walking to school when she found a wallet.","The detective knew the answer because he had found a footprint.","As the sun was setting, the camels reached the oasis.","Nobody knew that the old man had hidden the treasure."],"common_errors":["✗ While I walked home, I was hearing a noise. → ✓ While I was walking home, I heard a noise. (Long action → past continuous; short → past simple.)","✗ When the lights went out, I read a book. (in progress) → ✓ When the lights went out, I was reading a book. (Action in progress → past continuous.)","✗ When I arrived, they already left. → ✓ When I arrived, they had already left. (Earlier event → past perfect.)","✗ When I was cooking, the phone was ringing. → ✓ While I was cooking, the phone rang. (Short interrupting action → past simple.)"],"arabic":"الماضي البسيط للأحداث الرئيسة بالترتيب، والماضي المستمر للخلفية والحدث الجاري، والماضي التام للحدث الأسبق.\nwhen مع الحدث القصير المقاطع، وwhile مع الحدث الطويل الجاري: While we were walking home, we heard a noise.\nI was reading when the lights went out = كنت أقرأ عندما انطفأت الأضواء."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Was Raining When… Narrative Tenses”. Let’s learn narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U4-LS2 | It Was Raining When… Narrative Tenses","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: It was getting dark. Suddenly, a door opened. Someone had left it unlocked. Nobody was watching when the vase fell. • We hadn't noticed the note. What were you doing when you heard the noise?","on_screen":"It was getting dark. Suddenly, a door opened. Someone had left it unlocked. | Nobody was watching when the vase fell. • We hadn't noticed the note. | What were you doing when you heard the noise?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Stories use three past tenses. The past simple tells the main events in order: The lights went out. Someone knocked on the door. The past continuous (was/were + -ing) describes the background or an action in progress when something else happened: It was raining. I was reading when the lights went out. Use while + past continuous for a longer action: While we were walking home, we heard a noise.","on_screen":"past simple → main events in order • past continuous → background / action in progress • past perfect → earlier event (flashback)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The wind was blowing, and the trees were shaking. I was sleeping when I heard a strange sound. While Saad was talking on the phone, someone took his bag.","on_screen":"The wind was blowing, and the trees were shaking. / I was sleeping when I heard a strange sound. / While Saad was talking on the phone, someone took his bag.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “While I walked home, I was hearing a noise.” That’s not right. We say: “While I was walking home, I heard a noise.” Long action → past continuous; short → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ While I walked home, I was hearing a noise.   ✓ While I was walking home, I heard a noise.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I was reading when the lights went out.\" Which action was longer? … Think! … Reading. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I was reading when the lights went out.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I was reading when the lights went out.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الماضي البسيط للأحداث الرئيسة بالترتيب، والماضي المستمر للخلفية والحدث الجاري، والماضي التام للحدث الأسبق.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: While I walked home, I was hearing a noise. — الصحيح: While I was walking home, I heard a noise.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I was reading when the lights went out."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I ___ TV when I heard a knock on the window.","options":["am watching","watched","was watching","had watched"],"answer":"was watching","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"While we were camping, a strange light ___ across the sky.","options":["moves","moved","had move","was moving at"],"answer":"moved","explanation":"Main event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"When the police arrived, the thieves ___.","options":["had escaped","have escaped","were escaping at","escape"],"answer":"had escaped","explanation":"Earlier event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"___ I was waiting for the bus, I saw my old teacher.","options":["During","Since","While","When I"],"answer":"While","explanation":"when (short action) / while (long action).","explanation_ar":"when أو while."},{"q":"It was a dark night. The wind ___, and the rain was falling.","options":["howls","howled at","had howl","was howling"],"answer":"was howling","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"The phone rang ___ I was in the shower.","options":["since","while","during","for"],"answer":"while","explanation":"when (short action) / while (long action).","explanation_ar":"when أو while."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the correct form: past simple, past continuous or past perfect. Word bank: had opened, was reading, saw","items":[{"q":"Lina ______ (read) a mystery novel when the power went off.","options":[],"answer":"was reading","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"When we got back, we saw that someone ______ (open) the gate.","options":[],"answer":"had opened","explanation":"Earlier event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"While Yusuf was riding his bike, he ______ (see) a fox.","options":[],"answer":"saw","explanation":"Main event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"While I cleaned my room, I found an old letter.","options":[],"answer":"While I was cleaning my room, I found an old letter.","explanation":"cleaned → was cleaning. Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: cleaned → was cleaning. الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"When the teacher came in, the students already sat down.","options":[],"answer":"When the teacher came in, the students had already sat down.","explanation":"already sat → had already sat. Earlier event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: already sat → had already sat. الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"When I was eating dinner, my uncle was calling.","options":[],"answer":"When I was eating dinner, my uncle called.","explanation":"was calling → called. Main event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: was calling → called. الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Continue the story sentences.","items":[{"q":"It was a cold, windy night, and ___.","options":[],"answer":"It was a cold, windy night, and the trees were moving in the dark.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I was walking home from school when ___.","options":[],"answer":"I was walking home from school when I saw a strange box on the pavement.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"While my parents were sleeping, ___.","options":[],"answer":"While my parents were sleeping, our cat knocked over a vase.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When I opened the door, I realized that ___.","options":[],"answer":"When I opened the door, I realized that someone had been in my room.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Suddenly, ___.","options":[],"answer":"Suddenly, the lights went out.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Story builder.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 background sentences (past continuous).","options":[],"answer":"The moon was shining. The dogs were barking in the distance.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 main events (past simple) with when or while.","options":[],"answer":"While I was looking out of the window, I saw a shadow. When it moved, I screamed. My father ran into the room.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a flashback sentence (past perfect) that explains the mystery.","options":[],"answer":"It was my brother – he had climbed the tree to get his ball.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"when we / arrive / the thief / already / escape"},{"cue":"by the time / the police / come / the shop / close"},{"cue":"she / realize / she / leave / her keys at home"},{"cue":"he / not / eat / anything / all day"},{"cue":"the door / be / open / because / someone / break / the lock"},{"cue":"after / they / find / the clue / they / call / the detective"},{"cue":"I / read / a mystery / when / the lights / go out"},{"cue":"while / we / walk / home / we / hear / a noise"},{"cue":"Had / you / ever / see / a ghost town / before?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What ___ you doing when the earthquake started?","options":["had","are","were","did"],"answer":"were","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["When I arrived at the party, everyone has already eaten.","When I arrived at the party, everyone had already eaten.","When I arrived at the party, everyone already ate.","When I arrived at the party, everyone was already eat."],"answer":"When I arrived at the party, everyone had already eaten.","explanation":"Earlier event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"","options":["While Hamad was fishing, he found an old coin.","While Hamad was fishing, he was find an old coin.","While Hamad had fished, he finds an old coin.","While Hamad fished, he was finding an old coin."],"answer":"While Hamad was fishing, he found an old coin.","explanation":"when (short action) / while (long action).","explanation_ar":"when أو while."},{"q":"The children ___ in the garden when it started to rain.","options":["played at","had play","were playing","are playing"],"answer":"were playing","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"She couldn't open the door because she ___ her key.","options":["has lost yesterday","loses","was losing","had lost"],"answer":"had lost","explanation":"Earlier event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"As we were driving through the desert, a sandstorm ___.","options":["was beginning at","began","begins","had begin"],"answer":"began","explanation":"Main event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ the detective was looking at the map, the suspect ran away.","options":["While","Since","When I","During"],"answer":"While","explanation":"when (short action) / while (long action).","explanation_ar":"when أو while."},{"q":"","options":["The streets were quiet, and the shops were closing.","The streets were quiet, and the shops was closing.","The streets were quiet, and the shops had closing.","The streets were quiet, and the shops closing."],"answer":"The streets were quiet, and the shops were closing.","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"When Noura found the note, she understood what ___.","options":["was happening at","happens","has happened","had happened"],"answer":"had happened","explanation":"Earlier event → past perfect.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"Which tense tells the main events of a story?","options":["the present perfect","the past perfect","the past simple","the past continuous"],"answer":"the past simple","explanation":"Main event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A story timeline on the board with three colors: blue background scene (it was raining, the wind was blowing), red main events (the lights went out, someone knocked), green earlier events (someone had cut the wire); Yusuf telling the story with a flashlight under his chin. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A story timeline on the board with three colors: blue background scene (it was raining, the wind was blowing), red main events (the lights went out, someone knocked), green earlier events (someone had cut the wire); Yusuf telling the story with a flashlight under his chin"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Mysteries”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events)"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows evidence (facts or things that show something is true); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing evidence: facts or things that show something is true"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows witness (a person who saw something happen); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing witness: a person who saw something happen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows solve (to find the answer to a problem or mystery); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing solve: to find the answer to a problem or mystery"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows disappear (to go away suddenly so you can't see it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing disappear: to go away suddenly so you can't see it"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W01","script":"evidence. evidence. There wasn't enough evidence.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W02","script":"witness. witness. A witness saw a man running away.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W03","script":"solve. solve. Noura solved the mystery in one day.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-W04","script":"disappear. disappear. My pen disappeared from my desk.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “It Was Raining When… Narrative Tenses”. Let’s learn narrative tenses: past simple (main events), past continuous (background and interrupted actions), past perfect (earlier events); when and while together. Remember these patterns: It was getting dark. Suddenly, a door opened. Someone had left it unlocked. Nobody was watching when the vase fell. • We hadn't noticed the note. What were you doing when you heard the noise? Stories use three past tenses. The past simple tells the main events in order: The lights went out. Someone knocked on the door. The past continuous (was/were + -ing) describes the background or an action in progress when something else happened: It was raining. I was reading when the lights went out. Use while + past continuous for a longer action: While we were walking home, we heard a noise. Here are some examples. The wind was blowing, and the trees were shaking. I was sleeping when I heard a strange sound. While Saad was talking on the phone, someone took his bag. Be careful! Some learners say: “While I walked home, I was hearing a noise.” That’s not right. We say: “While I was walking home, I heard a noise.” Long action → past continuous; short → past simple. Quick check: \"I was reading when the lights went out.\" Which action was longer? … Think! … Reading. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I was reading when the lights went out.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3","title":"Mysterious, Puzzled, Whispered: Mystery Adjectives and Verbs for \"Said\"","objectives":["Students will be able to use mystery adjectives and choose between -ed and -ing adjectives.","Students will be able to replace \"said\" with more exact reporting verbs.","I can describe a scene as \"mysterious\" or \"eerie\".","I can write \"she whispered\" or \"he admitted\" instead of \"said\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صفات الغموض والاختيار بين الصفات المنتهية بـ -ed و-ing.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استبدال said بأفعال نقل أدق.","أستطيع أن أصف مشهدًا بأنه mysterious أو eerie.","أستطيع أن أكتب she whispered أو he admitted بدلًا من said."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"investigate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛstəˌɡeɪt/","definition":"to try to find out the truth about something","arabic":"يحقّق في","example":"The police are investigating the case.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"mysterious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/mɪˈstɪriəs/","definition":"strange and hard to explain","arabic":"غامض","example":"We heard a mysterious noise at night.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"puzzled","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpʌzəld/","definition":"confused because you don't understand","arabic":"محتار","example":"Adam looked puzzled by the question.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"footprint","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfʊtˌprɪnt/","definition":"a mark left by a foot or shoe","arabic":"أثر قدم","example":"There were muddy footprints on the floor.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W04"},{"word":"whisper","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈwɪspɚ/","definition":"to speak very quietly","arabic":"يهمس","example":"\"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W05"},{"word":"suspicious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈspɪʃəs/","definition":"making you think something is wrong","arabic":"مثير للشك / مُريب","example":"A suspicious man was standing by the door.","image_id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"Mystery adjectives make a story exciting: mysterious (strange and hard to explain), suspicious (making you think something is wrong), eerie (strange and a little frightening), puzzled (confused), terrified (very afraid), curious (wanting to know).\n-ed adjectives describe how a person feels: I was puzzled. -ing adjectives describe the thing that causes the feeling: The question was puzzling. Also: terrified / terrifying, frightened / frightening, surprised / surprising, interested / interesting.\nInstead of said, use a verb that shows how or why someone spoke: whispered (quietly), shouted (loudly), replied (answered), explained (made clear), admitted (said something true but embarrassing), exclaimed (said with surprise), complained (said you're unhappy), suggested (gave an idea).\nCollocations/phrases: whispered • shouted • muttered • exclaimed (how loud / how strong) | asked • replied • explained • added (questions and answers) | admitted • complained • suggested • warned (why they spoke)","examples":["The old house looked mysterious in the moonlight.","A suspicious man was hiding behind the car.","The empty street was eerie at midnight.","The detective was puzzled by the strange clue.","The story was terrifying, and the children were terrified.","\"Don't make a sound,\" she whispered.","\"I broke the vase,\" Adam admitted.","\"Let's follow the footprints,\" Sara suggested."],"common_errors":["✗ I was very puzzling by the question. → ✓ I was very puzzled by the question. (A person's feeling → -ed.)","✗ The film was terrified. → ✓ The film was terrifying. (The thing that causes the feeling → -ing.)","✗ \"Where are you?\" she replied. (it's a question) → ✓ \"Where are you?\" she asked. (A question → asked.)","✗ He said me the answer. → ✓ He told me the answer. / He said the answer to me. (say vs tell.)"],"arabic":"صفات الغموض: mysterious (غامض) وsuspicious (مريب) وeerie (موحش ومخيف قليلًا) وpuzzled (محتار) وterrified (مذعور).\nالصفة المنتهية بـ ed تصف شعور الشخص (I was puzzled)، والمنتهية بـ ing تصف الشيء المسبب للشعور (The question was puzzling).\nبدلًا من said نستخدم: whispered (همس) وshouted (صرخ) وreplied (ردّ) وadmitted (اعترف) وsuggested (اقترح)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Mysterious, Puzzled, Whispered: Mystery Adjectives and Verbs for \"Said\"”. Let’s learn mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U4-LS3 | Mysterious, Puzzled, Whispered: Mystery Adjectives and Verbs for \"Said\"","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. investigate: to try to find out the truth about something. mysterious: strange and hard to explain. puzzled: confused because you don't understand.","on_screen":"investigate | mysterious | puzzled","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Mystery adjectives make a story exciting: mysterious (strange and hard to explain), suspicious (making you think something is wrong), eerie (strange and a little frightening), puzzled (confused), terrified (very afraid), curious (wanting to know). -ed adjectives describe how a person feels: I was puzzled. -ing adjectives describe the thing that causes the feeling: The question was puzzling. Also: terrified / terrifying, frightened / frightening, surprised / surprising, interested / interesting.","on_screen":"mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The old house looked mysterious in the moonlight. A suspicious man was hiding behind the car. The empty street was eerie at midnight.","on_screen":"The old house looked mysterious in the moonlight. / A suspicious man was hiding behind the car. / The empty street was eerie at midnight.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I was very puzzling by the question.” That’s not right. We say: “I was very puzzled by the question.” A person's feeling → -ed.","on_screen":"✗ I was very puzzling by the question.   ✓ I was very puzzled by the question.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The story was terrifying.\" Who was afraid? … Think! … The readers – the story *caused* the fear. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a scene as \"mysterious\" or \"eerie\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a scene as \"mysterious\" or \"eerie\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","صفات الغموض: mysterious (غامض) وsuspicious (مريب) وeerie (موحش ومخيف قليلًا) وpuzzled (محتار) وterrified (مذعور).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I was very puzzling by the question. — الصحيح: I was very puzzled by the question.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف مشهدًا بأنه mysterious أو eerie."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The old house at the end of the street was dark and ___.","options":["terrified","curious about","puzzled","mysterious"],"answer":"mysterious","explanation":"Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"The detective was ___ – he couldn't understand the clue.","options":["puzzled","puzzles","puzzling","puzzle"],"answer":"puzzled","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"The noise in the attic was ___. We all ran outside!","options":["terrify","terrified","terrifying","terrifies"],"answer":"terrifying","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"\"I took your pencil,\" Faisal ___. \"I'm sorry.\"","options":["exclaimed","whispered","admitted","replied"],"answer":"admitted","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"\"Shh! The baby is sleeping,\" Mom ___.","options":["complained","whispered","shouted","exclaimed"],"answer":"whispered","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"A man in dark glasses was watching the bank. He looked ___.","options":["puzzled","eerie-ed","terrified","suspicious"],"answer":"suspicious","explanation":"Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the reporting verb to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"replied","options":["said suddenly with surprise or excitement","gave an idea","said that you are not happy about something","said very loudly","answered a question","made something clear"],"answer":"answered a question","explanation":"replied → answered a question. Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"exclaimed","options":["said suddenly with surprise or excitement","gave an idea","said that you are not happy about something","said very loudly","answered a question","made something clear"],"answer":"said suddenly with surprise or excitement","explanation":"exclaimed → said suddenly with surprise or excitement. Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"complained","options":["said suddenly with surprise or excitement","gave an idea","said that you are not happy about something","said very loudly","answered a question","made something clear"],"answer":"said that you are not happy about something","explanation":"complained → said that you are not happy about something. Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"suggested","options":["said suddenly with surprise or excitement","gave an idea","said that you are not happy about something","said very loudly","answered a question","made something clear"],"answer":"gave an idea","explanation":"suggested → gave an idea. Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"explained","options":["said suddenly with surprise or excitement","gave an idea","said that you are not happy about something","said very loudly","answered a question","made something clear"],"answer":"made something clear","explanation":"explained → made something clear. Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"shouted","options":["said suddenly with surprise or excitement","gave an idea","said that you are not happy about something","said very loudly","answered a question","made something clear"],"answer":"said very loudly","explanation":"shouted → said very loudly. Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Make your writing stronger.","items":[{"q":"Rewrite with a better verb: \"Help!\" he said.","options":[],"answer":"\"Help!\" he shouted.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Rewrite with a better verb: \"The soup is cold,\" she said.","options":[],"answer":"\"The soup is cold,\" she complained.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"eerie\".","options":[],"answer":"The empty school was eerie at night.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with \"surprised\" and \"surprising\".","options":[],"answer":"I was surprised by the ending. The ending was surprising.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe a suspicious person in one sentence.","options":[],"answer":"A suspicious man kept looking at his watch and at the door.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Mystery scene.","items":[{"q":"Describe a mysterious place in 2 sentences using 3 adjectives from the lesson.","options":[],"answer":"The old fort was eerie and silent. We saw mysterious lights in one of the towers.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a short dialogue (3 lines) with 3 different reporting verbs.","options":[],"answer":"\"Did you hear that?\" Lina whispered. \"It's just the wind,\" Sara replied. \"No, it's footsteps!\" Lina exclaimed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with an -ed adjective and one with an -ing adjective.","options":[],"answer":"We were terrified. The sound was terrifying.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"mystery","match":"something strange that nobody can explain","arabic":"لُغز / غموض"},{"word":"clue","match":"a piece of information that helps you find an answer","arabic":"دليل / مفتاح للحل"},{"word":"detective","match":"a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries","arabic":"محقّق"},{"word":"suspect","match":"a person who might have done something wrong","arabic":"مشتبه به"},{"word":"evidence","match":"facts or things that show something is true","arabic":"دليل / بيِّنة"},{"word":"witness","match":"a person who saw something happen","arabic":"شاهد"},{"word":"solve","match":"to find the answer to a problem or mystery","arabic":"يحلّ"},{"word":"disappear","match":"to go away suddenly so you can't see it","arabic":"يختفي"},{"word":"investigate","match":"to try to find out the truth about something","arabic":"يحقّق في"},{"word":"mysterious","match":"strange and hard to explain","arabic":"غامض"},{"word":"puzzled","match":"confused because you don't understand","arabic":"محتار"},{"word":"footprint","match":"a mark left by a foot or shoe","arabic":"أثر قدم"},{"word":"whisper","match":"to speak very quietly","arabic":"يهمس"},{"word":"suspicious","match":"making you think something is wrong","arabic":"مثير للشك / مُريب"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The ___ lights in the desert scared the campers.","options":["mysterious","puzzled","terrified","interested"],"answer":"mysterious","explanation":"Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"I was ___ by the strange message. I didn't understand it.","options":["puzzle","puzzling","puzzlement","puzzled"],"answer":"puzzled","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"The ending of the story was very ___. Nobody expected it.","options":["surprising","surprised","surprises","surprise"],"answer":"surprising","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"\"Can I help you?\" the shopkeeper ___.","options":["complained","admitted","asked","replied"],"answer":"asked","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"\"Yes, I saw him at nine,\" the witness ___.","options":["asked","exclaimed out","whispered to","replied"],"answer":"replied","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"\"Why don't we look in the garden?\" Saad ___.","options":["shouted at","suggested","admitted","complained"],"answer":"suggested","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"The empty hospital at night was strange and a little frightening – it was ___.","options":["eerie","curious","honest","puzzled"],"answer":"eerie","explanation":"Choose the mystery word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["The children were fright by the storm.","The children were frightened by the storm.","The children were frightening by the storm.","The children were frightens by the storm."],"answer":"The children were frightened by the storm.","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"\"We won!\" the captain ___ happily.","options":["admitted","exclaimed","complained","whispered"],"answer":"exclaimed","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"Someone who saw a crime happen is a ___.","options":["detective","suspect","witness","clue"],"answer":"witness","explanation":"Choose the mystery word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"An old abandoned house at dusk with a creaking gate and one lit window; three friends at the gate, one whispering, one looking terrified, one pointing at mysterious footprints; speech bubbles labeled \"whispered\", \"exclaimed\", \"admitted\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"An old abandoned house at dusk with a creaking gate and one lit window; three friends at the gate, one whispering, one looking terrified, one pointing at mysterious footprints; speech bubbles labeled \"whispered\", \"exclaimed\", \"admitted\""},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows investigate (to try to find out the truth about something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing investigate: to try to find out the truth about something"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mysterious (strange and hard to explain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mysterious: strange and hard to explain"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows puzzled (confused because you don't understand); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing puzzled: confused because you don't understand"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows footprint (a mark left by a foot or shoe); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing footprint: a mark left by a foot or shoe"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows whisper (to speak very quietly); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing whisper: to speak very quietly"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows suspicious (making you think something is wrong); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing suspicious: making you think something is wrong"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W01","script":"investigate. investigate. The police are investigating the case.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W02","script":"mysterious. mysterious. We heard a mysterious noise at night.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W03","script":"puzzled. puzzled. Adam looked puzzled by the question.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W04","script":"footprint. footprint. There were muddy footprints on the floor.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W05","script":"whisper. whisper. \"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-W06","script":"suspicious. suspicious. A suspicious man was standing by the door.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Mysterious, Puzzled, Whispered: Mystery Adjectives and Verbs for \"Said\"”. Let’s learn mystery adjectives (mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, terrified, eerie, strange); -ed vs -ing adjectives (puzzled/puzzling, terrified/terrifying); reporting verbs instead of \"said\" (whispered, shouted, replied, explained, admitted, exclaimed, complained, suggested) together. Meet some new words. investigate: to try to find out the truth about something. mysterious: strange and hard to explain. puzzled: confused because you don't understand. Mystery adjectives make a story exciting: mysterious (strange and hard to explain), suspicious (making you think something is wrong), eerie (strange and a little frightening), puzzled (confused), terrified (very afraid), curious (wanting to know). -ed adjectives describe how a person feels: I was puzzled. -ing adjectives describe the thing that causes the feeling: The question was puzzling. Also: terrified / terrifying, frightened / frightening, surprised / surprising, interested / interesting. Here are some examples. The old house looked mysterious in the moonlight. A suspicious man was hiding behind the car. The empty street was eerie at midnight. Be careful! Some learners say: “I was very puzzling by the question.” That’s not right. We say: “I was very puzzled by the question.” A person's feeling → -ed. Quick check: \"The story was terrifying.\" Who was afraid? … Think! … The readers – the story *caused* the fear. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a scene as \"mysterious\" or \"eerie\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4","title":"\"Look!\" She Whispered: Punctuating Dialogue","objectives":["Students will be able to punctuate dialogue with quotation marks, commas and end marks in the correct place.","Students will be able to start a new paragraph when a new person speaks.","I can write \"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","I can write Adam asked, \"Where is the key?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من ترقيم الحوار بعلامات التنصيص والفواصل وعلامات النهاية في المكان الصحيح.","سيتمكن الطلاب من بدء فقرة جديدة عندما يتحدث شخص جديد.","أستطيع أن أكتب \"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","أستطيع أن أكتب Adam asked, \"Where is the key?\""],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mystery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɪstɚi/","definition":"something strange that nobody can explain","arabic":"لُغز / غموض","example":"The disappearance of the ship is still a mystery.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"clue","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klu/","definition":"a piece of information that helps you find an answer","arabic":"دليل / مفتاح للحل","example":"The detective found an important clue.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"detective","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈtɛktɪv/","definition":"a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries","arabic":"محقّق","example":"The detective asked everyone questions.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"suspect","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səˈspɛkt/","definition":"a person who might have done something wrong","arabic":"مشتبه به","example":"The police questioned three suspects.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"evidence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛvədəns/","definition":"facts or things that show something is true","arabic":"دليل / بيِّنة","example":"There wasn't enough evidence.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"witness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɪtnəs/","definition":"a person who saw something happen","arabic":"شاهد","example":"A witness saw a man running away.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Put the exact words someone says inside quotation marks (\"…\"). Start the quotation with a capital letter: Adam said, \"The door is open.\"\nIn American English, commas and periods go inside the closing quotation mark. If the reporting words come after the quote, end the quote with a comma (not a period): \"The door is open,\" Adam said. If the quote is a question or an exclamation, use ? or ! inside the marks: \"Who's there?\" she asked. \"Run!\" he shouted.\nIf the reporting words come before the quote, put a comma after them: Noura asked, \"Had anyone visited the library?\" Start a new paragraph every time a different person speaks.\n\"Quote,\" he said. (comma inside)\nHe said, \"Quote.\" (comma before, period inside)\n\"Question?\" she asked. • \"Exclamation!\" he shouted.\ncapital letter at the start of the quote • new speaker = new paragraph","examples":["\"I found a clue,\" Noura said.","Ms. Huda said, \"I locked the case last night.\"","\"Where were you at eight o'clock?\" the detective asked.","\"Look out!\" Saad shouted.","Adam whispered, \"Did you hear that?\"","\"It's just the wind,\" Lina replied.","\"We need more evidence,\" the detective explained.","The witness said, \"The man was wearing a blue cap.\""],"common_errors":["✗ \"I'm hungry.\" she said. → ✓ \"I'm hungry,\" she said. (Reporting words after → comma, not period.)","✗ \"Where is it\"? he asked. → ✓ \"Where is it?\" he asked. (The question mark goes inside.)","✗ He said \"the door is open.\" → ✓ He said, \"The door is open.\" (Comma before the quote + capital letter.)","✗ \"Are you OK?\" She asked. → ✓ \"Are you OK?\" she asked. (she continues the sentence → small letter.)"],"arabic":"نضع الكلام المنقول حرفيًّا بين علامتي تنصيص ونبدأه بحرف كبير.\nفي الإنجليزية الأمريكية تأتي الفاصلة والنقطة داخل علامة التنصيص: \"The door is open,\" Adam said.\nإذا كان الكلام سؤالًا أو تعجبًا نضع ? أو ! داخل العلامة: \"Who's there?\" she asked.\nإذا جاء القائل أولًا نضع فاصلة بعده: Noura asked, \"Had anyone visited the library?\" ونبدأ فقرة جديدة لكل متكلم جديد."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “\"Look!\" She Whispered: Punctuating Dialogue”. Let’s learn quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U4-LS4 | \"Look!\" She Whispered: Punctuating Dialogue","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Put the exact words someone says inside quotation marks (\"…\"). Start the quotation with a capital letter: Adam said, \"The door is open.\"","on_screen":"quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Put the exact words someone says inside quotation marks (\"…\"). Start the quotation with a capital letter: Adam said, \"The door is open.\" In American English, commas and periods go inside the closing quotation mark. If the reporting words come after the quote, end the quote with a comma (not a period): \"The door is open,\" Adam said. If the quote is a question or an exclamation, use ? or ! inside the marks: \"Who's there?\" she asked. \"Run!\" he shouted.","on_screen":"\"Quote,\" he said. (comma inside) • He said, \"Quote.\" (comma before, period inside) • \"Question?\" she asked. • \"Exclamation!\" he shouted.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. \"I found a clue,\" Noura said. Ms. Huda said, \"I locked the case last night.\" \"Where were you at eight o'clock?\" the detective asked.","on_screen":"\"I found a clue,\" Noura said. / Ms. Huda said, \"I locked the case last night.\" / \"Where were you at eight o'clock?\" the detective asked.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “\"I'm hungry.\" she said.” That’s not right. We say: “\"I'm hungry,\" she said.” Reporting words after → comma, not period.","on_screen":"✗ \"I'm hungry.\" she said.   ✓ \"I'm hungry,\" she said.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I'm here.\" she said – what's wrong? … Think! … It needs a comma: \"I'm here,\" she said. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نضع الكلام المنقول حرفيًّا بين علامتي تنصيص ونبدأه بحرف كبير.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: \"I'm hungry.\" she said. — الصحيح: \"I'm hungry,\" she said.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب \"Look behind you,\" she whispered."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Missing Phone (editing passage)","body":"\"My phone has disappeared.\" Yusuf said. Noura asked \"When did you last see it?\" \"i left it on my desk before lunch\". \"Look under your bag\"! Lina exclaimed. \"It's right there!\" Yusuf laughed and said \"Thanks, Lina!\"","word_count":37,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correctly punctuated sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["\"The window is open.\" Ms. Huda said.","\"The window is open,\" Ms. Huda said.","The window is open, \"Ms. Huda said.\"","\"The window is open\", Ms. Huda said."],"answer":"\"The window is open,\" Ms. Huda said.","explanation":"Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["\"Who took the manuscript?,\" Noura asked.","\"Who took the manuscript\"? Noura asked.","\"Who took the manuscript?\" Noura asked.","\"Who took the manuscript.\" Noura asked?"],"answer":"\"Who took the manuscript?\" Noura asked.","explanation":"? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["Adam said \"I didn't touch anything.\"","Adam said, \"i didn't touch anything.\"","Adam said, I didn't touch anything.","Adam said, \"I didn't touch anything.\""],"answer":"Adam said, \"I didn't touch anything.\"","explanation":"Reporting words first → comma, then capital letter.","explanation_ar":"القائل أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["\"Run!\" the detective shouted.","\"Run,\" the detective shouted!","\"Run\"! the detective shouted.","\"Run!\" The detective shouted."],"answer":"\"Run!\" the detective shouted.","explanation":"Small letter for he/she after the quote; capital at the start of the quote.","explanation_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة."},{"q":"","options":["Lina whispered \"look at the footprints.\"","Lina whispered, \"Look at the footprints\".","Lina whispered, \"Look at the footprints.\"","Lina whispered, Look at the footprints."],"answer":"Lina whispered, \"Look at the footprints.\"","explanation":"Reporting words first → comma, then capital letter.","explanation_ar":"القائل أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"When do we start a new paragraph in a dialogue?","options":["only at the end of the story","when a different person speaks","after every question mark","after every comma"],"answer":"when a different person speaks","explanation":"New speaker → new paragraph.","explanation_ar":"متكلم جديد ← فقرة جديدة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add the punctuation. Write the sentence.","items":[{"q":"I saw a shadow Sara said  (punctuation)","options":[],"answer":"\"I saw a shadow,\" Sara said.","explanation":"Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"Is anyone there he asked  (punctuation)","options":[],"answer":"\"Is anyone there?\" he asked.","explanation":"? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"The witness said the car was red  (punctuation)","options":[],"answer":"The witness said, \"The car was red.\"","explanation":"Reporting words first → comma, then capital letter.","explanation_ar":"القائل أولًا ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"\"It's late.\" she said.","options":[],"answer":"\"It's late,\" she said.","explanation":"It's late.\" she → It's late,\" she. Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: It's late.\" she → It's late,\" she. الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"\"Where's the key\"? Omar asked.","options":[],"answer":"\"Where's the key?\" Omar asked.","explanation":"\"? → ?\". ? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: \"? → ?\". علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"\"Stop that man!\" She shouted.","options":[],"answer":"\"Stop that man!\" she shouted.","explanation":"She → she. Small letter for he/she after the quote; capital at the start of the quote.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: She → she. الحروف الكبيرة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the dialogue.","items":[{"q":"\"My phone has disappeared.\" Yusuf said.","options":[],"answer":"\"My phone has disappeared,\" Yusuf said.","explanation":".\" → ,\". Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: .\" → ,\". الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"Noura asked \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","options":[],"answer":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"i left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","options":[],"answer":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","explanation":"i → I. Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: i → I. الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch\". \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","options":[],"answer":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","explanation":"\". → .\". Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: \". → .\". الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag\"! Lina exclaimed.","options":[],"answer":"Noura asked, \"When did you last see it?\" \"I left it on my desk before lunch.\" \"Look under your bag!\" Lina exclaimed.","explanation":"\"! → !\". Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: \"! → !\". الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"\"It's right there!\" Yusuf laughed and said \"Thanks, Lina!\"","options":[],"answer":"\"It's right there!\" Yusuf laughed and said, \"Thanks, Lina!\"","explanation":"said \"Thanks → said, \"Thanks. Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: said \"Thanks → said, \"Thanks. الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write a mini dialogue.","items":[{"q":"Write a line with the reporting words after the quote.","options":[],"answer":"\"I heard a strange noise,\" Faisal whispered.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a question with the reporting words after it.","options":[],"answer":"\"Did you lock the door?\" Dad asked.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a line with the reporting words before the quote.","options":[],"answer":"Mom replied, \"Yes, I locked it at ten.\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"mystery","clue":"something strange that nobody can explain"},{"word":"detective","clue":"a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries"},{"word":"evidence","clue":"facts or things that show something is true"},{"word":"witness","clue":"a person who saw something happen"},{"word":"mysterious","clue":"strange and hard to explain"},{"word":"suspicious","clue":"making you think something is wrong"},{"word":"clue","clue":"a piece of information that helps you find an answer"},{"word":"suspect","clue":"a person who might have done something wrong"},{"word":"solve","clue":"to find the answer to a problem or mystery"},{"word":"disappear","clue":"to go away suddenly so you can't see it"},{"word":"investigate","clue":"to try to find out the truth about something"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["\"I'm not afraid.\" Rakan said.","\"I'm not afraid,\" Rakan said\".","\"I'm not afraid,\" Rakan said.","\"I'm not afraid\", Rakan said."],"answer":"\"I'm not afraid,\" Rakan said.","explanation":"Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["\"Did you see the light\"? Lina asked.","\"Did you see the light,\" Lina asked?","\"Did you see the light?\" Lina asked?","\"Did you see the light?\" Lina asked."],"answer":"\"Did you see the light?\" Lina asked.","explanation":"? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["The detective explained \"the thief came in through the window.\"","The detective explained, \"The thief came in through the window.\"","The detective explained, The thief came in through the window.","The detective explained, \"the thief came in through the window.\""],"answer":"The detective explained, \"The thief came in through the window.\"","explanation":"Reporting words first → comma, then capital letter.","explanation_ar":"القائل أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["\"Help!\" she screamed.","\"Help!\" She screamed.","\"Help\"! she screamed.","\"Help,\" She screamed!"],"answer":"\"Help!\" she screamed.","explanation":"Small letter for he/she after the quote; capital at the start of the quote.","explanation_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"We found it\" Saad said.","options":["after \"it\", inside the quotation marks","after \"Saad\"","after \"said\"","after \"We\""],"answer":"after \"it\", inside the quotation marks","explanation":"Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["Noura replied, No, I didn't see anyone.","Noura replied, \"no, I didn't see anyone.\"","Noura replied, \"No, I didn't see anyone.\"","Noura replied \"No, I didn't see anyone.\""],"answer":"Noura replied, \"No, I didn't see anyone.\"","explanation":"Reporting words first → comma, then capital letter.","explanation_ar":"القائل أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["\"Follow me.\" the guide whispered.","\"Follow me,\" the guide whispered.","Follow me, \"the guide whispered.\"","\"Follow me\", the guide whispered."],"answer":"\"Follow me,\" the guide whispered.","explanation":"Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"Which words need capital letters? he said, \"the box is empty.\"","options":["said","box","he and the","empty"],"answer":"he and the","explanation":"Small letter for he/she after the quote; capital at the start of the quote.","explanation_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة."},{"q":"","options":["\"Where were you last night.\" the officer asked?","\"Where were you last night\"? the officer asked.","\"Where were you last night,\" The officer asked.","\"Where were you last night?\" the officer asked."],"answer":"\"Where were you last night?\" the officer asked.","explanation":"? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"In a story, Sara speaks, and then Adam answers. What should the writer do?","options":["put Adam's words in brackets","use no quotation marks for Adam","put both in one sentence","start a new paragraph for Adam"],"answer":"start a new paragraph for Adam","explanation":"New speaker → new paragraph.","explanation_ar":"متكلم جديد ← فقرة جديدة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Mysteries” that shows quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Mysteries” that shows quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker in action"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “\"Look!\" She Whispered: Punctuating Dialogue”. Let’s learn quotation marks; commas, periods, question marks and exclamation marks inside the quotation marks (American English); capital letters at the start of a quotation; reporting clause before or after; a new paragraph for each new speaker together. Put the exact words someone says inside quotation marks (\"…\"). Start the quotation with a capital letter: Adam said, \"The door is open.\" Put the exact words someone says inside quotation marks (\"…\"). Start the quotation with a capital letter: Adam said, \"The door is open.\" In American English, commas and periods go inside the closing quotation mark. If the reporting words come after the quote, end the quote with a comma (not a period): \"The door is open,\" Adam said. If the quote is a question or an exclamation, use ? or ! inside the marks: \"Who's there?\" she asked. \"Run!\" he shouted. Here are some examples. \"I found a clue,\" Noura said. Ms. Huda said, \"I locked the case last night.\" \"Where were you at eight o'clock?\" the detective asked. Be careful! Some learners say: “\"I'm hungry.\" she said.” That’s not right. We say: “\"I'm hungry,\" she said.” Reporting words after → comma, not period. Quick check: \"I'm here.\" she said – what's wrong? … Think! … It needs a comma: \"I'm here,\" she said. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5","title":"My Mystery Story: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to tell and solve a mystery in groups.","Students will be able to write a short mystery story with narrative tenses and correctly punctuated dialogue.","I can solve a mystery with my group.","I can write a short mystery story with dialogue."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من رواية لغز وحلّه في مجموعات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة قصة غامضة قصيرة بأزمنة السرد وحوار صحيح الترقيم.","أستطيع أن أحلّ لغزًا مع مجموعتي.","أستطيع أن أكتب قصة غامضة قصيرة فيها حوار."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"mystery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɪstɚi/","definition":"something strange that nobody can explain","arabic":"لُغز / غموض","example":"The disappearance of the ship is still a mystery.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"clue","pos":"noun","ipa":"/klu/","definition":"a piece of information that helps you find an answer","arabic":"دليل / مفتاح للحل","example":"The detective found an important clue.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"detective","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dɪˈtɛktɪv/","definition":"a person whose job is to solve crimes or mysteries","arabic":"محقّق","example":"The detective asked everyone questions.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"suspect","pos":"noun","ipa":"/səˈspɛkt/","definition":"a person who might have done something wrong","arabic":"مشتبه به","example":"The police questioned three suspects.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"evidence","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛvədəns/","definition":"facts or things that show something is true","arabic":"دليل / بيِّنة","example":"There wasn't enough evidence.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"witness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɪtnəs/","definition":"a person who saw something happen","arabic":"شاهد","example":"A witness saw a man running away.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"solve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɑlv/","definition":"to find the answer to a problem or mystery","arabic":"يحلّ","example":"Noura solved the mystery in one day.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"disappear","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌdɪsəˈpɪr/","definition":"to go away suddenly so you can't see it","arabic":"يختفي","example":"My pen disappeared from my desk.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"investigate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛstəˌɡeɪt/","definition":"to try to find out the truth about something","arabic":"يحقّق في","example":"The police are investigating the case.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mysterious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/mɪˈstɪriəs/","definition":"strange and hard to explain","arabic":"غامض","example":"We heard a mysterious noise at night.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"puzzled","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpʌzəld/","definition":"confused because you don't understand","arabic":"محتار","example":"Adam looked puzzled by the question.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"footprint","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfʊtˌprɪnt/","definition":"a mark left by a foot or shoe","arabic":"أثر قدم","example":"There were muddy footprints on the floor.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"whisper","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈwɪspɚ/","definition":"to speak very quietly","arabic":"يهمس","example":"\"Look behind you,\" she whispered.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"suspicious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/səˈspɪʃəs/","definition":"making you think something is wrong","arabic":"مثير للشك / مُريب","example":"A suspicious man was standing by the door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\" and dialogue punctuation.\nA good mystery story has a setting (past continuous), a problem (past simple), clues, dialogue and a solution that goes back in time (past perfect).\n✔ past continuous → setting; past simple → events\n✔ past perfect → the earlier cause (had left, had flown)\n✔ mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, eerie, terrified\n✔ \"…,\" he whispered. • She asked, \"…?\"","examples":["The rain was falling, and the streets were empty.","Suddenly, the lights went out.","Someone had cut the power cable.","\"Stay where you are,\" the guard warned.","The house looked eerie in the dark.","\"I think I know the answer,\" Sara said quietly.","Adam admitted, \"I forgot to close the door.\"","The detective was puzzled by the mysterious note."],"common_errors":["✗ When I got there, the thief escaped already. → ✓ When I got there, the thief had already escaped. (Earlier event → past perfect.)","✗ \"Who is it\"? she asked. → ✓ \"Who is it?\" she asked. (? inside the quotation marks.)","✗ The noise was terrified. → ✓ The noise was terrifying. (Cause → -ing.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الماضي التام وأزمنة السرد وصفات الغموض وبدائل said وترقيم الحوار.\nالقصة الغامضة الجيدة فيها مكان وزمان، ومشكلة، وأدلة، وحوار، وحلّ يعود إلى حدث أسبق بالماضي التام.\nتذكّر: الفاصلة والنقطة وعلامة السؤال داخل علامات التنصيص."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Mystery Story: Language in Use”. Let’s learn past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L06-U4-LS5 | My Mystery Story: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Mystery club: each group gets a case card (The Missing Trophy, The Empty Lunchbox, The Locked Classroom). Students ask yes/no questions with the past perfect (Had someone…?) and past continuous (Was anyone…?) until they solve the mystery. Then they retell the solution.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\" and dialogue punctuation. A good mystery story has a setting (past continuous), a problem (past simple), clues, dialogue and a solution that goes back in time (past perfect).","on_screen":"✔ past continuous → setting; past simple → events • ✔ past perfect → the earlier cause (had left, had flown) • ✔ mysterious, suspicious, puzzled, eerie, terrified","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The rain was falling, and the streets were empty. Suddenly, the lights went out. Someone had cut the power cable.","on_screen":"The rain was falling, and the streets were empty. / Suddenly, the lights went out. / Someone had cut the power cable.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “When I got there, the thief escaped already.” That’s not right. We say: “When I got there, the thief had already escaped.” Earlier event → past perfect.","on_screen":"✗ When I got there, the thief escaped already.   ✓ When I got there, the thief had already escaped.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “\"Who is it\"? she asked.”? … Think! … It should be “\"Who is it?\" she asked.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can solve a mystery with my group.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can solve a mystery with my group.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الماضي التام وأزمنة السرد وصفات الغموض وبدائل said وترقيم الحوار.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: When I got there, the thief escaped already. — الصحيح: When I got there, the thief had already escaped.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أحلّ لغزًا مع مجموعتي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar","body":"It was a hot afternoon, and the students were playing football in the yard.\nWhen Yusuf went back to class, he found that someone had opened his lunchbox. His sandwich had disappeared!\n\"Who took my lunch?\" he shouted.\nEveryone looked puzzled. \"I was in the library all morning,\" Lina explained.\nThen Adam noticed something suspicious: a trail of crumbs led to the open window.\n\"Look!\" he whispered. On the windowsill, a fat pigeon was finishing the last piece of bread.\nThe class laughed. Yusuf had left the window open, and the bird had flown in.\n\"Well, at least the mystery is solved,\" Yusuf admitted with a smile.","word_count":107,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Omar's story. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The students were playing football in the yard.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Someone had eaten Yusuf's apple.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Lina said she had been in the library.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam found a trail of crumbs.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"A cat had taken the sandwich.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf had closed the window before he left.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Empty Lunchbox – by Omar”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"It was a hot afternoon, and the students ___ football.","options":["are playing","played at","were playing","had play"],"answer":"were playing","explanation":"Narrative tenses (past simple / past continuous / past perfect).","explanation_ar":"أزمنة السرد."},{"q":"When Yusuf went back to class, someone ___ his lunchbox.","options":["had opened","opens","has opened","had open"],"answer":"had opened","explanation":"Narrative tenses (past simple / past continuous / past perfect).","explanation_ar":"أزمنة السرد."},{"q":"Everyone looked ___.","options":["puzzling","puzzle","puzzles","puzzled"],"answer":"puzzled","explanation":"Mystery adjective / -ed or -ing.","explanation_ar":"صفات الغموض."},{"q":"\"Look!\" he ___.","options":["complained","whispered","replied","admitted to"],"answer":"whispered","explanation":"Verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"","options":["\"Who took my lunch?\" He shouted.","\"Who took my lunch?\" he shouted.","\"Who took my lunch\"? he shouted.","\"Who took my lunch,\" he shouted?"],"answer":"\"Who took my lunch?\" he shouted.","explanation":"Dialogue punctuation.","explanation_ar":"ترقيم الحوار."},{"q":"Yusuf had left the window open, and the bird ___ in.","options":["flies","had flew","has flown","had flown"],"answer":"had flown","explanation":"Narrative tenses (past simple / past continuous / past perfect).","explanation_ar":"أزمنة السرد."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Solve a case with your group.","items":[{"q":"Your case: ___","options":[],"answer":"The Missing Trophy","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question 1 (Had someone…?): ___","options":[],"answer":"Had someone moved the trophy before the ceremony?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question 2 (Was anyone…?): ___","options":[],"answer":"Was anyone cleaning the hall in the morning?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The clue that solved it: ___","options":[],"answer":"The cleaner had put the trophy in a cupboard to polish it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Retell the solution in 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"While the students were having lunch, the cleaner was polishing the trophy. He had taken it to the storeroom, so nobody had stolen it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your mystery story.","items":[{"q":"Plan: setting, problem, 2 clues, dialogue, solution (past perfect).","options":[],"answer":"setting: windy night at my grandpa's farm; problem: the camel was missing; clues: broken fence, footprints to the oasis; dialogue: Grandpa, my cousin, me; solution: the wind had broken the fence, and the camel had walked to the water","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your story in 8–10 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"It was a windy night, and we were sleeping at my grandpa's farm. In the morning, Grandpa shouted, \"The camel has disappeared!\" We were puzzled. My cousin noticed something suspicious. \"Look, the fence is broken,\" he whispered. We followed some large footprints across the sand. They led to a small oasis. There, the camel was drinking water calmly. The strong wind had broken the fence, and the thirsty camel had walked to the water. \"Mystery solved!\" I exclaimed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: tenses? quotation marks? commas inside? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"Look, the fence is broken\". he whispered to \"Look, the fence is broken,\" he whispered.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"mystery","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"clue","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"detective","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"suspect","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"evidence","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"witness","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"solve","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"disappear","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"investigate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mysterious","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"puzzled","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"footprint","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"whisper","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"suspicious","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The moon ___, and the owls were calling in the trees.","options":["shines","was shining","had shine","shined at"],"answer":"was shining","explanation":"Narrative tenses (past simple / past continuous / past perfect).","explanation_ar":"أزمنة السرد."},{"q":"When the guard checked the safe, the jewels ___.","options":["had disappeared","had disappear","disappear","have disappeared"],"answer":"had disappeared","explanation":"Narrative tenses (past simple / past continuous / past perfect).","explanation_ar":"أزمنة السرد."},{"q":"","options":["While we were exploring the cave, we found an old map.","While we were exploring the cave, we were find an old map.","While we explored the cave, we were finding an old map.","While we had explored the cave, we find an old map."],"answer":"While we were exploring the cave, we found an old map.","explanation":"Narrative tenses (past simple / past continuous / past perfect).","explanation_ar":"أزمنة السرد."},{"q":"The ___ house had broken windows and no lights.","options":["puzzled","eerie","terrified","interested"],"answer":"eerie","explanation":"Mystery adjective / -ed or -ing.","explanation_ar":"صفات الغموض."},{"q":"The ending of the film was ___.","options":["shocked","shock","shocks","shocking"],"answer":"shocking","explanation":"Mystery adjective / -ed or -ing.","explanation_ar":"صفات الغموض."},{"q":"\"I'm sorry – I lost your book,\" Hamad ___.","options":["exclaimed","replied to","whispered at","admitted"],"answer":"admitted","explanation":"Verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"\"Why don't we call the police?\" Sara ___.","options":["complained","suggested","admitted","shouted at"],"answer":"suggested","explanation":"Verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"","options":["The guard warned, Don't touch the glass.","The guard warned \"don't touch the glass.\"","The guard warned, \"don't touch the glass\".","The guard warned, \"Don't touch the glass.\""],"answer":"The guard warned, \"Don't touch the glass.\"","explanation":"Dialogue punctuation.","explanation_ar":"ترقيم الحوار."},{"q":"","options":["It's locked, \"Omar said.\"","\"It's locked.\" Omar said.","\"It's locked,\" Omar said.","\"It's locked\", Omar said."],"answer":"\"It's locked,\" Omar said.","explanation":"Dialogue punctuation.","explanation_ar":"ترقيم الحوار."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a mystery story:","options":["\"Someone had been here before us.\" the detective whispered.","\"Someone had be here before us,\" The detective whispered.","\"Someone had been here before us,\" the detective whispered.","\"Someone has been here before us\" the detective whispered."],"answer":"\"Someone had been here before us,\" the detective whispered.","explanation":"Dialogue punctuation.","explanation_ar":"ترقيم الحوار."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A \"Mystery Club\" corner in the classroom: a cork board with photos, string and clue cards; Omar, Sara and Adam in detective hats reading a case file; a story draft with colorful quotation marks. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A \"Mystery Club\" corner in the classroom: a cork board with photos, string and clue cards; Omar, Sara and Adam in detective hats reading a case file; a story draft with colorful quotation marks"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Mysteries”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as teenagers aged 14–17, realistic proportions, modern school/city settings. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Mysteries”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L06-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS5-T1","script":"It was a hot afternoon, and the students were playing football in the yard. When Yusuf went back to class, he found that someone had opened his lunchbox. His sandwich had disappeared! \"Who took my lunch?\" he shouted. Everyone looked puzzled. \"I was in the library all morning,\" Lina explained. Then Adam noticed something suspicious: a trail of crumbs led to the open window. \"Look!\" he whispered. On the windowsill, a fat pigeon was finishing the last piece of bread. The class laughed. Yusuf had left the window open, and the bird had flown in. \"Well, at least the mystery is solved,\" Yusuf admitted with a smile.","voice":"en-US, natural young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L06-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Mystery Story: Language in Use”. Let’s learn past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\", dialogue punctuation (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Mystery club: each group gets a case card (The Missing Trophy, The Empty Lunchbox, The Locked Classroom). Students ask yes/no questions with the past perfect (Had someone…?) and past continuous (Was anyone…?) until they solve the mystery. Then they retell the solution. Today you use all of Unit 4: the past perfect, narrative tenses, mystery adjectives, verbs instead of \"said\" and dialogue punctuation. A good mystery story has a setting (past continuous), a problem (past simple), clues, dialogue and a solution that goes back in time (past perfect). Here are some examples. The rain was falling, and the streets were empty. Suddenly, the lights went out. Someone had cut the power cable. Be careful! Some learners say: “When I got there, the thief escaped already.” That’s not right. We say: “When I got there, the thief had already escaped.” Earlier event → past perfect. Quick check: what is wrong with “\"Who is it\"? she asked.”? … Think! … It should be “\"Who is it?\" she asked.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can solve a mystery with my group.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"When I got to the classroom, the lesson ___.","options":["had already start","has already started","had already started","already starts"],"answer":"had already started","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"","options":["She hadn't saw the message before the meeting.","She haven't seen the message before the meeting.","She didn't had seen the message before the meeting.","She hadn't seen the message before the meeting."],"answer":"She hadn't seen the message before the meeting.","explanation":"hadn't + past participle.","explanation_ar":"النفي."},{"q":"___ the visitors left before the storm began?","options":["Were","Did","Have","Had"],"answer":"Had","explanation":"Had + subject + past participle?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"By the time the firefighters came, the neighbors ___ the fire.","options":["have put out","had put out","had put outed","put out at"],"answer":"had put out","explanation":"by the time / already / never + past perfect.","explanation_ar":"by the time."},{"q":"","options":["The witness has noticed a white van last night.","The witness had noticed a white van yesterday at now.","The witness had noticed a white van.","The witness had notice a white van."],"answer":"The witness had noticed a white van.","explanation":"had + past participle (gone, seen, left).","explanation_ar":"الصيغة."},{"q":"I ___ in the garden when I heard a scream.","options":["am sitting","was sitting","had sit","sat at"],"answer":"was sitting","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"While the family was having dinner, the doorbell ___.","options":["had ring","rings","was ringing at","rang"],"answer":"rang","explanation":"Main event → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الرئيس ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"When we came back, we saw that somebody ___ our tent.","options":["had moved","has moved yesterday","was moving at","moves"],"answer":"had moved","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"___ Lina was reading, her little brother hid her glasses.","options":["Since","During","While","When I"],"answer":"While","explanation":"when (short action) / while (long action).","explanation_ar":"when أو while."},{"q":"The sky was dark, and thunder ___ in the distance.","options":["rumbled at","was rumbling","rumbles","had rumble"],"answer":"was rumbling","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."},{"q":"The police officer looked at the ___ car parked outside the bank.","options":["puzzled","suspicious","curious-ed","terrified"],"answer":"suspicious","explanation":"Choose the mystery adjective with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"صفة الغموض."},{"q":"The strange message left everyone ___.","options":["puzzled","puzzle","puzzling","puzzles"],"answer":"puzzled","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"The movie was so ___ that I couldn't sleep.","options":["frightening","fright","frightens","frightened"],"answer":"frightening","explanation":"-ed (feeling) vs -ing (cause).","explanation_ar":"ed أم ing."},{"q":"\"I didn't do my homework,\" Rakan ___.","options":["replied to","exclaimed","whispered at","admitted"],"answer":"admitted","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"\"Wow, what a goal!\" the commentator ___.","options":["whispered to","complained","exclaimed","admitted"],"answer":"exclaimed","explanation":"Choose the best verb instead of \"said\".","explanation_ar":"بديل said."},{"q":"A person who might be guilty is a ___.","options":["suspect","footprint","detective","witness"],"answer":"suspect","explanation":"Choose the mystery word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["\"The safe is empty.\" the guard said.","\"The safe is empty,\" the guard said.","\"The safe is empty\", the guard said.","The safe is empty, \"the guard said.\""],"answer":"\"The safe is empty,\" the guard said.","explanation":"Comma inside the quote before the reporting verb.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة داخل علامة التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["\"Where did you find it?\" Noura asked?","\"Where did you find it\"? Noura asked.","\"Where did you find it?\" Noura asked.","\"Where did you find it,\" Noura asked."],"answer":"\"Where did you find it?\" Noura asked.","explanation":"? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"","options":["The coach shouted, Keep running!","The coach shouted, \"Keep running!\"","The coach shouted, \"keep running\"!","The coach shouted \"keep running!\""],"answer":"The coach shouted, \"Keep running!\"","explanation":"Reporting words first → comma, then capital letter.","explanation_ar":"القائل أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["\"Watch out!\" he warned.","\"Watch out!\" He warned.","\"Watch out,\" He warned!","\"Watch out\"! he warned."],"answer":"\"Watch out!\" he warned.","explanation":"Small letter for he/she after the quote; capital at the start of the quote.","explanation_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة."},{"q":"In a dialogue, when should you start a new paragraph?","options":["each time a new person speaks","after every sentence","only when someone asks a question","never"],"answer":"each time a new person speaks","explanation":"New speaker → new paragraph.","explanation_ar":"متكلم جديد ← فقرة جديدة."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a mystery story.","options":["When we returned, someone had open the gate, and the garden were eerily quiet.","When we returned, someone has opened the gate, and the garden was eerily quietly.","When we returned, someone opened already the gate, and the garden was eerie quiet.","When we returned, someone had opened the gate, and the garden was eerily quiet."],"answer":"When we returned, someone had opened the gate, and the garden was eerily quiet.","explanation":"Earlier past action → had + past participle.","explanation_ar":"الحدث الأسبق ← الماضي التام."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"where had you been\"? the detective asked.","options":["\"Where had you been?\" The detective asked.","\"Where had you been\"? the detective asked.","\"where had you been?\" the detective asked.","\"Where had you been?\" the detective asked."],"answer":"\"Where had you been?\" the detective asked.","explanation":"? or ! inside the quotation marks.","explanation_ar":"علامة السؤال داخل التنصيص."},{"q":"What were you doing when the lights went out? – ___","options":["I read a mystery novel in my room at.","I had reading a mystery novel in my room.","I was reading a mystery novel in my room.","I was read a mystery novel in my room."],"answer":"I was reading a mystery novel in my room.","explanation":"Background / in progress → past continuous.","explanation_ar":"الخلفية ← الماضي المستمر."}],"theme_ar":"الألغاز","essential_question_ar":"كيف نصل إلى الحقيقة عندما لا تكون الأمور كما تبدو؟","can_do":"I can tell a mystery story with narrative tenses including the past perfect, use mystery adjectives and verbs for reporting speech, and punctuate dialogue correctly.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أروي قصة غامضة بأزمنة السرد ومنها الماضي التام، وأستخدم صفات الغموض وأفعالًا بديلة لـ said، وأضع علامات الترقيم في الحوار بشكل صحيح."});
